                <pb facs="0162" n="74" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg74"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 763.72/9: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace to the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-01-10T18:00:00+00:00"
                            >January 10, 1919—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>229. Your 119, January 6th, 9 p.m. Commission agrees with the suggestion that
                    Department make reply to the German proposal along lines adopted by British and
                    French Governments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>] <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Mission</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
